# {{ project_name }}

A Databricks Genie Space project scaffolded by [dex](https://github.com/yarrib/dex).

Genie Spaces are conversational AI/BI interfaces that let users ask natural language questions
about your data. This bundle provisions a Genie space backed by Unity Catalog tables and
{% if include_sample_instructions %}pre-loaded with curated SQL instructions{% else %}ready for your SQL instructions{% endif %}.

## Setup

```bash
uv sync
```

Configure your Databricks CLI profile:

```bash
databricks configure
```

## Deploy

```bash
# Deploy to dev (default target)
databricks bundle deploy

# Deploy to staging
databricks bundle deploy --target staging

# Deploy to prod
databricks bundle deploy --target prod
```

After deploying, open the Databricks workspace and navigate to **AI/BI > Genie** to find your
space.

## Customize

### Adding tables

Edit `resources/{{ project_name }}_genie_space.yml` and add entries under `tables:`:

```yaml
tables:
  - catalog_name: ${var.catalog}
    schema_name: ${var.schema}
    table_name: my_table
```

### Adding SQL instructions
{% if include_sample_instructions %}
Edit `src/{{ project_name }}/instructions/curated_questions.md` to add pre-validated questions
and SQL hints. Genie uses these to answer natural language questions more accurately.
{% else %}
Create a Markdown file with curated questions and SQL hints, then reference it with
`instructions_file_path` in the Genie space resource YAML.
{% endif %}

### Setting the warehouse

Set `warehouse_id` in your bundle variables or update the resource YAML directly:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --var="warehouse_id=<your-warehouse-id>"
```

## Development

```bash
# Run tests
uv run pytest

# Lint
uv run ruff check .

# Format
uv run ruff format .
```

